.TH tucsplit n 0.23.0 tclutils "Tcl Library Procedures"
.SH NAME
tucsplit \- Split text files by content markers, similar in spirit to csplit.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf
package require tclutils::tucsplit
.fi
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
set files [::tclutils::tucsplit::file handbook.md {^# } \-outdir chapters \-prefix chapter \-suffix .md]
.fi
.PP
By default, a matching line starts the next part and is kept in that part.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP
\fBsplitText text pattern ?options?\fR
.IP
\fBfile path pattern ?options?\fR
.PP
Options include \fB\-regexp\fR, \fB\-keepmatch\fR, \fB\-prefix\fR, \fB\-suffix\fR, \fB\-outdir\fR, \fB\-digits\fR, and \fB\-empty\fR.

